    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d892">

                <pb facs="1167" n="1157" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Sturgeon, Leo D.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-23T09:00:00+07:00">March 23, 1946—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 23—6:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>545. Reasons given by Sturgeon for unauthorized withdrawal from Dairen
                    (Shanghai’s 468, March 20 to Department repeated Chungking 213) are not
                    considered by Embassy as satisfactory explanation for his action. There is
                    nothing in Embassy’s confidential instruction mentioned by Sturgeon (namely,
                    Embassy’s 141, February 27, to Shanghai repeated Department 378<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d892-f1"/>) which would in any way [have] authorized him voluntarily
                    to withdraw without specific orders. Embassy is at a loss to understand his
                    hasty departure from Dairen and withdrawal of all personnel with him after
                    considerable effort expended in establishing him there.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
